 ## Unreleased — 1.4.0
 
-Nothing yet.
+### `fmt` no longer re-parses its own output
+
+`cmd_fmt` dropped the runtime round-trip guard that re-parsed the canonical text it had
+just written and compared the result back against the input, on every file, on every run.
+The guard could only ever catch a defect in `write_surface` itself — no document a user
+could supply reached it — so it bought no protection a test suite could not already give,
+at the cost of a full second parse per file. The property is now asserted once, at the
+library level: `every_accepted_mutation_round_trips` and `versioning.rs` in
+`crates/smysl-core/tests` fuzz `write_surface`'s output and assert it re-parses to the same
+records and declared version. `fmt` no longer exits `9`; that code is now `reindex
+--verify`'s alone.
 
